          "text": "{\"schema_version\":\"ai-evaluator-v2/1.1\",\"case_id\":\"2-1\",\"candidate_id\":\"candidate_3\",\"action_assessment\":{\"status\":\"defect\",\"summary\":\"Many source actions are present, but the resource-restoration path omits the required Service Management problem-resolution-report handling before Customer Service continuation, and some branch-specific action meaning is distorted.\"},\"flow_assessment\":{\"status\":\"defect\",\"summary\":\"Required precedence is broken in key places: after re-prioritization the process should continue to the detailed problem report but instead terminates, and the final Customer Service tasks are forced into an unsupported sequence rather than remaining unordered/concurrent.\"},\"control_flow_assessment\":{\"status\":\"defect\",\"summary\":\"Major routing errors exist: the Service-Management-can-analyze branch is wrongly continued into Resource Provisioning, the re-prioritization branch terminates instead of rejoining, the restoration branch skips the required Service Management resolution path, and the final concurrent work is modeled sequentially.\"},\"main_error_type\":\"mixed_or_cascading\",\"explanation\":\"The graph captures much of the overall skeleton, but several central behaviors are not preserved. In the source, if customer significance affects measures, the process is re-prioritized and then continues to detailed reporting; here that branch ends at the final node. In the source, when Service Management can analyze the problem itself, it analyzes and creates a trouble report without sending the case through Resource Provisioning; here that branch is merged into the Resource Provisioning detection flow. In the automatic restoration case, the source requires the trouble-shooting report to return to Service Management and feed creation/sending of the problem resolution report to Customer Service; here the graph jumps directly to the final customer-reporting section. The source also requires two concurrent Customer Service activities, but the graph serializes them. These defects affect multiple major branches and materially change continuation, branching, and outcomes.\" ,\"overall_score\":0.44,\"severity\":\"major\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"ambiguity_flag\":false,\"ambiguity_explanation\":\"\",\"requires_human_review\":false,\"review_reason\":\"\"}"
        }
